From 9fb9b2a17312fef4d897f875203c4953d0105780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:42:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T1694: the day's question never asks the same fact about a
 person twice

Lika's report, 13 Oct (seat 160584): on 12 Oct the day's question asked
where a contact works. She answered in full: he used to work at one firm and
has gone to Europe to study. That was kept as a past role and a note, so the
employer field stayed empty, and on 13 Oct the same question was asked again.
The queue now reads which facts it has already asked this owner about each
person (curiosity_surfacing_log) and moves to the next missing one. A person
whose every missing fact has been asked about drops out. Whatever the owner
said is the answer, even when it fills no field. No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
